\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Biden Criticizes Ruling In Florida on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Rogers \par \uc2 918 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 April 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 12\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The president's campaign moved to pin responsibility squarely on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after the Florida Supreme Court cleared the way for a six-week ban.\par \par \uc2 President Biden on Tuesday called a decision by the Florida Supreme Court to uphold a restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law ''outrageous'' and ''extreme,'' saying that it had effectively eliminated access to the procedure across the American South.\par \par \uc2 The president said in a statement that the restrictions in Florida and others enacted by Republicans across the country ''are putting the health and lives of millions of women at risk.'' But Mr. Biden said voters would ''have the opportunity to make their voices heard,'' after the court ruled separately that Floridians would be able to decide on expanding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in November.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's statement on the decision, which clears the way for a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, came as his campaign and a host of Democratic officials began an all-out effort to pin responsibility for dwindling access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care squarely on former President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ''\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is directly to blame for the fact that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now been effectively banned across the entire Southeastern United States,'' Julie Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez, Mr. Biden's campaign manager, told reporters on Tuesday. ''Make no mistake, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will do everything in his power to try and enact a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if he's re-elected.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump has indicated support for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban of around 15 weeks, with exceptions for rape or incest, or to save the mother's life. A representative for the Trump campaign did not immediately respond to a request for comment on the Florida decision.\par \par \uc2 Democrats believe the Florida decisions will turn out voters and perhaps even flip the state -- a long shot in a state where Mr. Biden's opponent is a registered voter.\par \par \uc2 ''We're cleareyed about how hard it will be to win Florida,'' Ms. Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez said, ''but we also know that Trump does not have it in the bag.''\par \par \uc2 As evidence, she and other officials pointed to ballot initiatives in states where voters have chosen to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade in 2022. The court's decision, which ended the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , followed Mr. Trump's appointment of three conservative justices.\par \par \uc2 The decision in Florida puts intense scrutiny on a state that has historically been a haven for people from states with more restrictive measures who are seeking abortions. The state's conservative-leaning Supreme Court ruled on Monday that a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban enacted in 2022 was constitutional. That ruling will allow a six-week ban championed by \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Florida's Republican governor, to take effect by May 1. Mr. Trump previously called the six-week ban a ''terrible mistake.''\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the court also ruled that a proposed constitutional amendment guaranteeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights until fetal viability, usually around 24 weeks, could go on the November ballot.\par \par \uc2 Democrats say curtailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is a losing issue for Republicans. In Congress, some Republicans, particularly those in swing districts, have quietly stepped away from restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation, instead trying to attack Democrats on issues like immigration, crime and the economy.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, on Tuesday, Mr. Trump's campaign shared the names and photos of people officials said had been victims of crimes by undocumented immigrants as the former president prepared to visit Michigan and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Democrats stayed focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ''The more Republicans do here, the worse it's going to get for them at the ballot box, as it should, because this is an issue people care about all across the country,'' said Gov. Roy Cooper, Democrat of North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign also released an ad in battleground states on Tuesday in which the president accused his competitor of supporting a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. It opens with Mr. Trump saying he was ''proud'' to have helped overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 ''\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn't trust women,'' Mr. Biden says in the ad. ''I do.''\par \par \uc2 The spot is part of a $30 million expenditure on advertising in competitive states. Viewers will see it during Major League Baseball games, ''Saturday Night Live'' and prime-time programming including the Country Music Television awards, the campaign said. The campaign is also targeting social media platforms, including \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , \uc2 YouTube\uc2  and \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , so Florida-based users will see it.\par \par \uc2 People familiar with the Biden campaign's strategy said it was unclear whether the campaign would put significant resources toward flipping Florida, but several said the court's decision allowing a referendum on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights would draw voters to the polls. Recent polling shows that there is enough support for the measure to pass, a sign that activists say is encouraging months before the election.\par \par \uc2 ''I think in this election cycle, with these contrasts, everything is possible, and we have to run everywhere like it's possible,'' \uc2 Mini Timmaraju\uc2 , the president of \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2 , said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden, a practicing Catholic, has been a reluctant supporter of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, framing the issue around personal privacy and civil rights rather than access to a medical procedure. On Tuesday, he did not use the word ''\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 '' in his statement.\par \par \uc2 ''Vice President Harris and I stand with the vast majority of Americans who support a woman's right to choose, including in Florida,'' he said.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A12. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240403ek430003b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
