\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Democrat Who Spoke Out For  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access Wins Alabama State House Seat\b0\par\par\uc2 By Maggie Astor \par \uc2 574 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 March 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 13\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Marilyn Lands flipped a State House seat in the deep-red state by 25 percentage points, underscoring the continued political potency of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Marilyn Lands, a Democrat, won a special election Tuesday for a State House seat in Alabama after campaigning on access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and in vitro fertilization, underscoring the continued political potency of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lands defeated her Republican opponent, Teddy Powell, by about 25 percentage points -- an extraordinary margin in a swing district where she lost by seven points in 2022. The special election was called when David Cole, the Republican who had held the seat, resigned and pleaded guilty to voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 ''Today, Alabama women and families sent a clear message that will be heard in Montgomery and across the nation,'' Ms. Lands, a licensed counselor, said Tuesday night. ''Our legislature must repeal Alabama's no-exceptions \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, fully restore access to I.V.F. and protect the right to contraception.''\par \par \uc2 Her election, in the largely suburban House District 10 in northern Alabama, does not change the balance of power in the state; Republicans still hold supermajorities in both its House and its Senate. And the race was small, with only about 6,000 votes cast.\par \par \uc2 But the outcome and the margin add further evidence to the pile of election results over the nearly two years since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and, now, I.V.F., is a reliably motivating issue. Democrats are counting on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in 2024 to continue to help power wins in key states.\par \par \uc2 Alabama has banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all stages of pregnancy, with no exceptions for rape and incest. And last month, the \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  ruled that frozen embryos were people with rights -- upending I.V.F. care, which typically involves creating multiple embryos but implanting only one at a time, and indefinitely freezing or sometimes destroying those left over.\par \par \uc2 In response to the backlash over that ruling, the Alabama Legislature passed a law giving I.V.F. clinics criminal and civil immunity and Gov. \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2 , a Republican, signed it. It did not address embryos' legal status.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Powell, the Republican candidate, avoided talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and I.V.F. during the campaign, focusing instead on issues including education and local infrastructure. That strategy, which many national candidates have also adopted over the past two years, does not appear to have been effective.\par \par \uc2 Heather Williams, the president of the Democratic Legislative Campaign Committee, which works to elect Democrats to state legislatures, called Ms. Lands's victory ''a harbinger of things to come.''\par \par \uc2 ''Republicans across the country have been put on notice that there are consequences to attacks on I.V.F.,'' Ms. Williams said.\par \par \uc2 President Biden's re-election campaign, which is planning to focus heavily on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well, also highlighted the result, calling it a ''major warning sign'' for former President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 . Mr. Trump, who appointed three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe, has indicated that he is likely to support a 15-week federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 ''Voters will not stand for his attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,'' Mr. Biden's campaign manager, Julie Chavez Rodriguez, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Marilyn Lands defeated her G.O.P. opponent by about 25 percentage points. This article appeared in print on page A13. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240328ek3s0004k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
